PThreadTicker
=============

Version 0.01, from UnixLib v5.0.1 (riscos-unixlib).

A small module that makes threaded UnixLib programs (built with GCCSDK
GCC 10 and UnixLib 5.0.1 or later: Warzone 2100, OpenTTD, SDL
programs...) safer in the desktop.

What it does
------------
UnixLib switches a program's threads with a timer that fires every
2 centiseconds. That timer can fire while another desktop task is
running, so the code it calls must always be in memory. PThreadTicker
holds that code. Without the module, UnixLib runs its own copy from the
RMA (module area), which also works today.

The module has no commands, SWIs or settings. UnixLib programs find it
by name and use it if it was loaded before they started.

Installing
----------
Either:
- merge the !System in this archive with yours (open !Boot, System,
  and drag this !System onto the merge window), then load it from a
  program's !Run file:
    RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
- or put PThrTicker inside an application and load it from its !Run:
    RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad <MyApp$Dir>.PThrTicker

*Help PThreadTicker shows the version.

Removing
--------
The module refuses to quit ("PThreadTicker is in use by UnixLib
programs") while a program is using it: quit those programs first. If a
program crashed while using it, it stays in use until the computer is
restarted. That is harmless.

Checking what it does
---------------------
  *Set UnixLib$TickerStats <Wimp$ScrapDir>.TickerStats
makes every UnixLib program append one line of timer counters to that
file when it quits. Lines ending via=module used this module.

